                <pb facs="0549" n="518" sameAs="frus:frus1969-76v40/pg518"/>

                <head>ANNEX II</head>
                <p>(Draft of written Soviet communication to the three Allied Ambassadors)</p>
                <p>The Government of the USSR, with the reference
                    to part II, section B (1) (D) of the quadripartite agreement of this date, and
                    after consultation thereon with the Government of the German Democratic
                    Republic, has the honor to bring to the attention of the Governments of the
                    French Republic, the United Kingdom and the United States of America the
                    following detailed arrangements concerning communication within the city and its
                    environs.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Permanent residents of the Western sectors will be able to visit the
                        environs of the city for compassionate, family, religious or cultural
                        reasons, or as tourists.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>The Western end of the Teltow Canal will be opened to navigation.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>Measures implementing the above arrangements will be worked out by the
                        appropriate German authorities in accordance with part II, section B (1) (D)
                        of the quadripartite agreement.</item>
                </list>
                <p rendition="#flush">(Signature)</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">(Date)</p>
            </div>
